---
// The legend for the grid cells: one line per answer, the same words the aria-labels and the status filter use.
// The three weaker answers belong to a country without a list (DESIGN.md §8d).
---
<p class="legend">
  <span class="rs-key"><span class="cl cl-yes">✓</span> fit: on the list (the hover says whether with a condition)</span>
  <span class="rs-key"><span class="cl cl-doc">✓</span> fit by the maker's document — the grid operator decides</span>
  <span class="rs-key"><span class="cl cl-else">○</span> accepted on other EU lists — nothing checked here</span>
  <span class="rs-key"><span class="cl cl-type">B</span> over the type-A limit: type B, a procedure of its own</span>
  <span class="rs-key"><span class="cl cl-no">✕</span> not fit: refused, expired or not allowed</span>
  <span class="rs-key"><span class="cl cl-free">—</span> nothing to check for this class</span>
  <span class="rs-key"><span class="cl cl-none"></span> not on the list, or nothing known — never “not approved”</span>
  <span class="small muted">Hover or focus a cell for the list's own word, a condition or date, firmware and the row.</span>
</p>
